 "blurb": "The picture as it looks after travelling down a composite video cable. Colour rides on a subcarrier inside the brightness signal, so dots crawl along colour edges, fine black and white stripes turn into shimmering rainbows, sharp edges ring, colour lags behind and smears sideways, and a little picture noise comes along. PAL flips part of its colour every line and averages pairs of lines, so it looks different from NTSC.",
